    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0246" n="144" xml:id="pg144"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5855: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan (Grew) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-03T12:00:00+09:00">February 3,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received February 3—12:44 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. Peiping’s 79 and 80 just received by mail.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d135-f1"/>
                    Guarded remarks of Japanese General Staff officers here to Military Attaché
                    yesterday indicate that Japanese Army hopes to reach arrangement regarding Jehol
                    by negotiations of some kind.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d135-f1" n="67" xml:id="d135-f1-content">
                <p>No. 79, dated January 23, 7 p.m., not printed; No. 80, dated January 24, 11 a.m.,
                    is printed on <ref target="#pg124">p. 124</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
